    "Features"
  ],
  "Body": {
    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>Data storage limits in <a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fazure.microsoft.com%2Fproducts%2Fazure-sql%2Fdatabase%2F%23overview&amp;data=04%7C01%7Cmoslake%40microsoft.com%7Ca5c6f9e0392242717b4008da06015858%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C637828900115272971%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&amp;sdata=BXHoDQqtjqUHSqgJtL5aUJScEPiVuC1VA5BcJbkZNMY%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Azure SQL Database</a> have increased from 1.5 TB to 2 TB for single databases and elastic pools configured with 8 and 10 vcores.&nbsp;Workloads requiring up to 2 TB storage can now reduce costs by not having to increase the compute size beyond 8 vcores.&nbsp;This increase applies to both serverless and provisioned compute in the General Purpose and Business Critical tiers.&nbsp;For more information on storage limits in Azure SQL Database, please refer to <a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.microsoft.com%2Fazure%2Fazure-sql%2Fdatabase%2Fresource-limits-vcore-single-databases&amp;data=04%7C01%7Cmoslake%40microsoft.com%7Ca5c6f9e0392242717b4008da06015858%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C637828900115272971%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&amp;sdata=S3dEt3w5W9BizDPZU0lMujIMkdlCWMZ4g6YUYXdLScg%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">single database vCore resource limits</a> and <a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.microsoft.com%2Fazure%2Fazure-sql%2Fdatabase%2Fresource-limits-vcore-elastic-pools&amp;data=04%7C01%7Cmoslake%40microsoft.com%7Ca5c6f9e0392242717b4008da06015858%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C637828900115272971%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&amp;sdata=jzaQuZRC9SHS%2BbPVJXb%2BIgpSfU7pOb5%2Fpi%2FFCx%2BeVNQ%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">elastic pool vCore resource limits</a>.</p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "Data storage limits in Azure SQL Database have increased from 1.5 TB to 2 TB for single databases and elastic pools configured with 8 and 10 vcores. Workloads requiring up to 2 TB storage can now reduce costs by not having to increase the compute size beyond 8 vcores. This increase applies to both serverless and provisioned compute in the General Purpose and Business Critical tiers. For more information on storage limits in Azure SQL Database, please refer to single database vCore resource limits and elastic pool vCore resource limits ."
  },
